---
import { readFile } from 'node:fs/promises';
import { resolve } from 'node:path';
import DefinitionHelp from './DefinitionHelp.astro';
import { INDEX_URL, INDEX_BYTE_LIMIT, VIEW_BYTE_LIMIT, parseJSONBytes, validateIndex, validateViewBundle, viewLabel, metricLabel, salaryCoverage, decimal, money, percentile, gapMultiple, gapScaleCopy, sortGapRows, millionSummary, readableReason, teamName, type Bundle } from './moneyball';
let data: Bundle | null = null;
let state = 'Reviewed salary and contribution records are not available. No player findings are shown.';
try {
  const rawIndex = await readFile(resolve(process.cwd(), `public${INDEX_URL}`));
  const index = validateIndex(parseJSONBytes(rawIndex, INDEX_BYTE_LIMIT));
  const initial = index.views.find(v => v.id === index.defaultView)!;
  const rawView = await readFile(resolve(process.cwd(), `public${initial.url}`));
  data = validateViewBundle(parseJSONBytes(rawView, VIEW_BYTE_LIMIT), initial, index.dataVersion);
  state = data.publication.status === 'private-preview' ? 'Private preview' : 'Reviewed export';
} catch (error) {
  if ((error as NodeJS.ErrnoException).code !== 'ENOENT') state = 'The player export failed validation. No results are shown; the export must be corrected.';
}
const defaultMillion = data ? millionSummary(data.views[0], 'war') : null;
---

<section id="mb-explorer" tabindex="-1" data-reference-target class="moneyball figure" aria-label="NBA salary and contribution explorer" data-moneyball>
  <a class="mb-skip" data-mb-skip href="#mb-explorer">Skip to basketball explorer</a>
  <form id="mb-controls" tabindex="-1" data-reference-target aria-label="Explore player value">
    <fieldset disabled data-mb-controls class="mb-controls">
      <legend class="mb-sr">Player comparison controls</legend>
      <div class="mb-primary">
        <div class="mb-search" data-mb-search-shell>
          <label for="mb-player-search">Search player <span class="mb-small">(2+ letters)</span></label>
          <div class="combobox-shell">
            <input type="search" id="mb-player-search" data-mb-search autocomplete="off" placeholder="Search by name" role="combobox" aria-autocomplete="list" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="mb-player-suggestions" aria-describedby="mb-search-result" />
            <div id="mb-player-suggestions" class="suggestion-menu" data-mb-suggestions role="listbox" aria-label="Matched players in this view" hidden></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <label>Contribution<select data-mb-metric><option value="war">Estimated wins (WAR)</option><option value="lebron">Impact when playing</option></select></label>
      </div>
      <div class="mb-visible-context">
        <label><span data-mb-season-label>Season</span><select data-mb-season aria-label="Season ending"><option value="">Awaiting data</option></select></label>
        <label>Team<select data-mb-team><option value="">All teams</option></select></label>
        <button type="button" data-mb-reset>Reset</button>
      </div>
      <p class="mb-small mb-search-instructions" data-mb-search-instructions></p>
      <p class="mb-sr" id="mb-search-result" role="status" aria-live="polite" data-mb-search-result></p>
      <div class="mb-secondary mb-salary-controls">
        <label>Salary units<select data-mb-units aria-describedby="mb-salary-help"><option value="usd">US dollars</option><option value="share">% of salary cap</option></select></label>
        <p class="mb-small" id="mb-salary-help"><DefinitionHelp id="mb-cap" label="Salary cap / share">Player salary divided by that season's NBA salary cap, shown as a percentage. The denominator is the league cap, not team payroll, the luxury-tax threshold or either apron. Multi-season dollars use the ending season's cap.</DefinitionHelp></p>
      </div>
      <details class="mb-filters" data-mb-context-controls>
        <summary>Time span</summary>
        <div class="mb-secondary">
          <label>Time span<select data-mb-window aria-describedby="mb-window-help"><option value="1">One season</option><option value="3">Three seasons</option><option value="5">Five seasons</option></select></label>
        </div>
        <p class="mb-small mb-note" id="mb-window-help">Multi-season views average across available matched seasons for each player; they are not period totals.</p>
      </details>
    </fieldset>
  </form>
  <figure aria-labelledby="mb-chart-title" aria-describedby="mb-chart-guide mb-caption">
    <h2 id="mb-chart-title" class="mb-sr">Explore player value</h2>
    <p id="mb-chart-guide" class="mb-guide" data-mb-guide hidden>Select a dot or search. <strong>Above the line:</strong> more than estimated at this pay; <strong>below:</strong> less. <a class="mb-ranked-link" href="#mb-ranked-records">Ranked comparisons</a></p>
    <div class="mb-chart-tools"><p class="mb-small"><span data-mb-status role="status" aria-live="polite">{state}</span><span data-mb-period></span></p></div>
    <section class="mb-team" data-mb-team-context hidden aria-label="Selected team scope and partial totals">
      <p class="mb-small" data-mb-team-scope></p>
      <dl class="mb-facts mb-team-facts" data-mb-team-summary></dl>
      <p class="mb-small" data-mb-team-basis></p>
    </section>
    <div class="mb-no-matches" data-mb-no-matches hidden><p>No players match this search.</p><button type="button" data-mb-clear-search>Clear search</button></div>
    <div class="mb-chart-layout">
      <div class="mb-plot">
        <p class="mb-axis mb-y"><span data-mb-war-help><DefinitionHelp id="mb-war" label="WAR">WAR estimates wins above a readily available fill-in player over playing time, including availability. Zero is that replacement baseline, not the team's actual wins.</DefinitionHelp></span><span data-mb-lebron-help hidden><DefinitionHelp id="mb-lebron" label="LEBRON">LEBRON is an impact statistic: it estimates on-court impact per 100 possessions. Zero means league-average impact; this is a rate, not points actually scored.</DefinitionHelp></span><span class="mb-axis-copy"><span data-mb-y-label>Estimated wins · season total</span><span data-mb-metric-note>Zero: a readily available fill-in player.</span></span></p>
        <div class="mb-stage">
          <svg role="img" data-mb-chart aria-label="Salary and measured contribution" viewBox="0 0 300 420"><title>No interactive records loaded</title></svg>
          <div class="mb-empty" data-mb-empty><h3 data-mb-empty-title>Player comparison unavailable</h3><p data-mb-empty-copy>Load a validated view or read the saved records below.</p><button type="button" data-mb-retry>Retry data</button></div>
        </div>
        <p class="mb-small mb-match-count" data-mb-count role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
        <p class="mb-axis mb-x" data-mb-x-label>Salary · US dollars</p>
      </div>
    <div class="mb-legend" aria-label="Chart legend"><button type="button" data-mb-find-player disabled>Find a player</button><span><i class="mb-dot-key" data-mb-peer-key aria-hidden="true"></i><DefinitionHelp id="mb-matched" label="Matched player">One player whose salary and contribution records cover the same seasons and pass the inclusion rules. Missing or ineligible records stay out of the comparison.</DefinitionHelp></span><span data-mb-selected-key hidden><i class="mb-selected-key" aria-hidden="true"></i>Selected player</span><span><i class="mb-line-key" aria-hidden="true"></i><DefinitionHelp id="mb-reference" label="Salary reference">The fitted league line estimates contribution at each salary. A player's comparison is the vertical gap from that line.</DefinitionHelp></span><span><i class="mb-band-key" aria-hidden="true"></i><DefinitionHelp id="mb-band" label="Reference range">The shading describes uncertainty in the fitted league line while treating player scores as fixed. It is not uncertainty in an individual player's impact.</DefinitionHelp></span></div>
      <section id="mb-player-comparison" class="mb-selection" aria-label="Selected player" data-mb-selection-panel tabindex="-1">
        <h3 data-mb-selection-name aria-live="polite" hidden>Player comparison</h3>
        <p class="mb-small" data-mb-selection-context hidden></p>
        <p data-mb-selection>Select a dot, choose an example or search for a player.</p>
        <div data-mb-comparison hidden>
          <p class="mb-small" data-mb-selected-unit></p>
          <dl class="mb-answer"><dt><DefinitionHelp id="mb-residual" label="Above / below salary reference">The player's measured contribution minus the league line at that pay. Positive is above the line; negative is below it.</DefinitionHelp></dt><dd><span data-mb-selected-gap></span> <small data-mb-selected-direction></small></dd></dl>
          <dl class="mb-comparison">
            <div><dt>Measured contribution</dt><dd data-mb-selected-contribution></dd></div>
            <div><dt>Reference at this pay</dt><dd data-mb-selected-reference></dd></div>
            <div><dt>Reported pay</dt><dd class="mb-pay-value"><span data-mb-selected-salary></span><p class="mb-small mb-pay-basis" data-mb-selected-salary-basis></p></dd></div>
          </dl>
          <p class="mb-small" data-mb-selected-observed hidden></p>
          <section class="mb-salary-prototype" data-mb-salary-prototype hidden aria-labelledby="mb-salary-prototype-title">
            <div class="mb-prototype-heading"><h4 id="mb-salary-prototype-title">Salary at this LEBRON level</h4><span class="mb-prototype-badge">Prototype</span></div>
            <p class="mb-small">At the same LEBRON, where does the league line meet the salary axis? This compares impact while playing, not recommended pay.</p>
            <label class="mb-connector-toggle"><input type="checkbox" data-mb-salary-connector checked /> Show horizontal line and reference square</label>
            <p class="mb-small" data-mb-salary-unavailable hidden></p>
            <button type="button" class="mb-salary-example" data-mb-salary-example hidden></button>
            <dl class="mb-prototype-result" data-mb-salary-result>
              <div><dt>Salary at the league line</dt><dd data-mb-salary-reference></dd></div>
              <div><dt>Difference from reported pay</dt><dd data-mb-salary-difference></dd></div>
            </dl>
            <p class="mb-small" data-mb-salary-basis></p>
            <p class="mb-small" data-mb-salary-exposure></p>
            <details class="mb-prototype-limit"><summary>How to read this prototype</summary>
              <p class="mb-small">The open square keeps the player's LEBRON fixed and meets the league line at a different salary. It translates the existing comparison into money; it adds no independent evidence of value.</p>
              <p class="mb-small">Annual pay also covers playing time. The same LEBRON can produce the same reference salary for players with very different minutes. LEBRON reflects role and team context, not pure talent or a fully healthy season.</p>
              <p class="mb-small">No salary uncertainty interval is calculated. Small changes in impact or the fitted line can change the dollar comparison substantially. Values are approximate; the shaded band still concerns contribution on the league line.</p>
              <p class="mb-small" data-mb-salary-sensitivity></p>
            </details>
          </section>
          <details class="mb-comparison-details" data-mb-comparison-details><summary>More comparison details</summary>
            <dl class="mb-pay-rank"><div><dt><DefinitionHelp id="mb-value-percentile" label="League gap percentile" detailTarget="mb-percentile-calculation" detailLabel="Full calculation">Ranks this gap relative to eligible matched league gaps, not as a player grade. Tied gaps share a midpoint rank.</DefinitionHelp></dt><dd data-mb-selected-percentile></dd></div></dl>
            <p class="mb-gap-size"><DefinitionHelp id="mb-gap-size" label="Gap size" detailTarget="mb-gap-size-calculation" detailLabel="Full calculation">+2× is a positive gap twice the typical league distance; negative is below the line and zero is on it. The typical distance is the median of matched players' distances on either side of the line.</DefinitionHelp> <span data-mb-selected-magnitude></span><br /><span data-mb-selected-scale></span></p>
            <p class="mb-small" data-mb-selected-cohort></p>
            <p class="mb-small">This ranks league gaps, not player quality. It does not tell you how unusual the gap is among players at similar pay.</p>
            <details class="mb-player-details"><summary>Playing time and records</summary><p class="mb-small" data-mb-selected-details></p></details>
          </details>
        </div>
        <a class="mb-controls-return" href="#mb-controls">Back to controls</a>
      </section>
      <div class="mb-examples" data-mb-examples hidden><span>Try:</span><div data-mb-example-buttons></div></div>
  <p class="mb-small mb-note" data-mb-window-note>One dot compares the same player's matched salary and contribution. Controls become available after the selected view passes validation.</p>
  <p class="mb-small mb-note" data-mb-coverage-summary></p>
    </div>

    <figcaption id="mb-caption" data-mb-caption hidden>League reference stays fixed under filters. Tap an underlined term for help; tap outside or press Escape to close.</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <details data-mb-live-table hidden class="mb-records">
    <summary id="mb-ranked-records" data-reference-target>Player records</summary>
    <p class="mb-small" data-mb-table-order>Ordered by the active contribution gap, highest first.</p>
    <p id="mb-scroll-help" class="mb-small">Scroll across for more columns and down for more players. <a href="#mb-about-title">Skip player rows to About</a>.</p>
    <div class="mb-table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Player records, scroll horizontally and vertically" aria-describedby="mb-scroll-help" tabindex="0">
      <table><caption class="mb-sr">Current matched player records. Select a name for details. The active contribution measure and its native gap are shown.</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Player</th><th scope="col" class="mb-number" data-mb-table-residual>Gap (WAR)</th><th scope="col" class="mb-number" data-mb-table-cost>Pay (USD)</th><th scope="col" class="mb-number" data-mb-table-contribution>WAR · season total</th><th scope="col">Teams</th><th scope="col"><DefinitionHelp id="mb-observed" label="Observed / window">The number of active matched seasons included for this player out of the selected span. A 2/3 entry uses two matched seasons within a three-season window; averages cover those two seasons.</DefinitionHelp></th></tr></thead><tbody data-mb-rows></tbody></table>
    </div>
  </details>
  <section data-mb-snapshot aria-labelledby="mb-snapshot-title" class="mb-snapshot">
    <h3 id="mb-snapshot-title" tabindex="-1">Saved {data ? viewLabel(data.views[0]) : 'default'} records</h3>
    {data ? <>
      <p class="mb-small">Saved {viewLabel(data.views[0])} records include both contribution measures and remain available without JavaScript. Other seasons and time spans load separately.</p>
      {data.views.map(v => <details>
        <summary>Player records · {viewLabel(v)}</summary>
        <p class="mb-small">{v.coverage.matched} matched salary records among {v.coverage.eligible} player records meeting playing-time and contribution-metric rules. {salaryCoverage(v)}{v.coverage.excluded.length > 0 && ` Primary exclusion reasons: ${v.coverage.excluded.map(e => `${e.count}: ${readableReason(e.reason)}`).join('; ')}`}</p>
        <p class="mb-small">{v.window === 1 ? 'One player-season per row; nominal annual compensation and season-total WAR.' : `Average annual end-season cap-equivalent compensation and WAR per observed matched active season; possession-weighted LEBRON. ${v.window} possible seasons per player.`} Negative contribution remains visible.</p>
        <div class="mb-table-scroll" role="region" aria-label={`${viewLabel(v)} player records, scroll horizontally`} tabindex="0">
          <table><caption>{viewLabel(v)} · complete matched export · WAR gap, highest first</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Player / NBA ID</th><th scope="col">Teams</th><th scope="col"><DefinitionHelp id={`mb-observed-build-${v.id}`} label="Observed seasons">The active matched seasons included for this player. The count after them gives observed seasons out of the selected window. Averages use the observed matched seasons.</DefinitionHelp></th><th scope="col">{v.window === 1 ? 'Compensation (USD)' : 'Avg compensation (end-cap USD)'}</th><th scope="col">% cap</th><th scope="col">LEBRON rate</th><th scope="col">LEBRON above / below reference</th><th scope="col">LEBRON Gap percentile</th><th scope="col">LEBRON gap size · × typical league gap</th><th scope="col">{v.window === 1 ? 'WAR total' : 'Avg WAR / observed season'}</th><th scope="col">WAR above / below reference</th><th scope="col">WAR Gap percentile</th><th scope="col">WAR gap size · × typical league gap</th><th scope="col">Evidence notes</th></tr></thead><tbody>{sortGapRows(v.players, 'war').map(p => <tr><th scope="row">{p.name}<small>{p.id}</small></th><td>{p.teams.join(', ')}</td><td>{p.observedSeasons.join(', ')} ({p.observedSeasons.length}/{v.window})</td><td>{money(p.salaryUsd)}</td><td>{decimal(p.salaryCapShare * 100)}%</td><td>{decimal(p.lebron)}</td><td>{decimal(p.residual.lebron)}</td><td>{percentile(p.valuePercentile.lebron)}</td><td>{gapMultiple(p.gapMultiple.lebron, false)}</td><td>{decimal(p.war)}</td><td>{decimal(p.residual.war)}</td><td>{percentile(p.valuePercentile.war)}</td><td>{gapMultiple(p.gapMultiple.war, false)}</td><td>{p.flags.length ? p.flags.map(readableReason).join('; ') : 'No additional flags supplied'}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table>
        </div>
        <details><summary>Team attribution and reference evidence</summary><p class="mb-small">Coverage note: {v.coverage.note}</p>
          {v.teams.map(t => <p class="mb-small">{teamName(t.team, v.endSeason)}: {t.status === 'unavailable' ? 'compensation and WAR unavailable' : `${money(t.salaryUsd!)} compensation; ${decimal(t.war!)} WAR`} {v.window > 1 ? 'per year over the full window' : 'in the season'}. {t.attributablePlayerSeasons}/{t.eligiblePlayerSeasons} matched player-seasons assigned to this club. Broader active-source audit: {t.excludedTradeCount} trade/unknown-allocation flags and {t.excludedMissingCount} missing-data flags. Those audit counts may overlap and include ineligible rows; they do not partition the matched sample. {t.note}</p>)}
          {(['lebron', 'war'] as const).map(m => <div><h4>{metricLabel(m, v)}</h4><p>{gapScaleCopy(m, v)}</p><dl class="mb-million-evidence"><dt>Model</dt><dd>{v.models[m].name}</dd><dt>Method</dt><dd>{v.models[m].method}</dd><dt>Validation</dt><dd><ul class="mb-validation-clauses" data-mb-saved-validation={m}>{v.models[m].validation.split(' | ').map(clause => <li>{clause}</li>)}</ul></dd><dt>Interval</dt><dd>{v.models[m].intervalLabel}</dd></dl></div>)}
        </details>
      </details>)}
    </> : <p>No reviewed records are available. Missing salary or contribution is never replaced with zero.</p>}
  </section>
  <section class="mb-methods" aria-labelledby="mb-about-title">
    <h2 id="mb-about-title" tabindex="-1" data-reference-target>About this comparison</h2>
    <details><summary>Reading the chart</summary>
      <p>Each dot is a player with matched salary and contribution records. The league line estimates contribution at that pay; the selected player's gap is the distance above or below it.</p>
      <p>WAR adds estimated wins above a readily available fill-in player over playing time. LEBRON measures impact per 100 possessions relative to league average, not points actually scored.</p>
      <p><a href="https://www.bball-index.com/lebron-introduction/" rel="noreferrer">Provider explanation of LEBRON and WAR</a>.</p>
      <p>Multi-season views average available matched seasons, not full-period totals. The selected player's observed-season count tells you how many seasons are included.</p>
      <p>In the LEBRON view, the optional horizontal connector holds the player's impact rate fixed and meets the league line at a comparison salary. It does not estimate deserved pay, what similar players earn, or what the player would contribute over a full season.</p>
    </details>
    <details><summary>Methods and limitations</summary>
      <p>A baseline, a straight line and a modest curve are checked on held-out players, with simpler fits retained when results are close. Rookie, minimum and maximum contract rules constrain pay, so this is a descriptive comparison.</p>
      <p class="mb-million-summary" data-mb-million-summary>{defaultMillion?.summary ?? 'The $1 million comparison is unavailable until a validated view loads.'}</p>
      <p>Salary and contribution cover the same matched seasons. Team totals cover only records that can be assigned to that club; they are not its full payroll or roster performance.</p>
      <p>The shaded range concerns the fitted league line, not uncertainty in an individual player's impact. These comparisons do not establish cause; gap percentile and Gap size describe league comparisons, not talent or significance.</p>
      <details class="mb-technical" data-mb-technical><summary>Technical records: current view and saved default</summary>
        <section id="mb-technical-records" tabindex="-1" data-reference-target>
          <h4>Current interactive view</h4>
          <dl class="mb-facts"><dt>View</dt><dd data-mb-view-context>No interactive view loaded.</dd><dt>Salary-reference model</dt><dd data-mb-view-model-name></dd><dt>Reference-range meaning</dt><dd data-mb-model></dd></dl>
          <h5>Current coverage: separate populations</h5>
          <dl class="mb-facts" data-mb-coverage-facts></dl>
          <p class="mb-small">Player counts, player-season counts and known-dollar totals describe different populations. Read each population separately; these rows are not consecutive steps in one exclusion total.</p>
          <h5>Reported exclusion counts</h5><dl class="mb-facts" data-mb-coverage-exclusions></dl>
          <details><summary>Exact current method, validation and source records</summary>
            <dl class="mb-million-evidence"><dt>View, model and version</dt><dd data-mb-view-evidence>No interactive view loaded.</dd><dt>Method</dt><dd data-mb-view-method></dd><dt>Validation</dt><dd><ul class="mb-validation-clauses" data-mb-view-validation></ul></dd><dt>Interval</dt><dd data-mb-view-interval></dd></dl>
            <p class="mb-small mb-coverage" data-mb-coverage>Interactive coverage appears after a view loads.</p>
            <section data-mb-team-audit-panel hidden><h5>Current team attribution audit</h5><p class="mb-small" data-mb-team-audit>No team audit loaded.</p></section>
            <h5>Current source retrieval dates and versions</h5><ul data-mb-view-source-versions></ul>
          </details>
          <h4>Representation and fitting</h4>
<p>The analysis fits a league-wide relationship between matched compensation and each contribution measure. The above / below reference value is the vertical gap between a player's dot and that curve. It stays fixed under team or player filters.</p><p>For multi-season windows, salary and both contribution measures cover exactly the same observed matched active seasons. A player can have fewer observed seasons than the selected window. Read that count beside the player before comparing averages. WAR and salary cap share average the observed matched active seasons; LEBRON uses the provider's possession counts as weights. Dollar views multiply average cap share by the ending-season salary cap. Team annual averages instead divide attributable player-season totals by the full selected window length.</p>{data && <><p>{data.definitions.eligibility}</p>{data.views.map(v => <details><summary>Saved {viewLabel(v)} model and validation</summary>{(['lebron', 'war'] as const).map(m => <dl class="mb-million-evidence"><dt>{m.toUpperCase()} model</dt><dd>{v.models[m].name}</dd><dt>Method</dt><dd>{v.models[m].method}</dd><dt>Validation</dt><dd><ul class="mb-validation-clauses" data-mb-saved-validation={m}>{v.models[m].validation.split(' | ').map(clause => <li>{clause}</li>)}</ul></dd></dl>)}</details>)}</>}
<h4>Salary and team attribution</h4>
<p>Salary cap share divides reported pay by that season's league cap, putting seasons on a common spending scale. Dollar views use nominal compensation for one season and ending-season cap-equivalent annual averages for multi-season windows.</p><p>Rookie scales, minimums and maximums constrain contracts; cap normalization preserves those constraints. Team membership shows the full player record. Team totals use only attributable matched salary and summed WAR, and show exclusions for traded or missing allocations. Rate values are never summed.</p>{data && <p>{data.definitions.salary}</p>}
<h4>Uncertainty and validation</h4>
<p>The shaded range describes how much the fitted league comparison varies when matched players are sampled again. It treats the supplied player scores as fixed and keeps the chosen type of curve. It does not measure uncertainty in a player's own impact, guarantee coverage of the whole curve at once, or include uncertainty from choosing the model. The extra-$1m range concerns the difference between two fitted points. These comparisons do not show that higher pay causes higher performance.</p>
      <h5>Uncertainty and validation records</h5>
        <p class="mb-small">Terms: <DefinitionHelp id="mb-case-bootstrap" label="case bootstrap">Draw players again from the matched cohort, allowing a player to appear more than once, and refit the salary reference. The supplied scores and chosen curve type stay fixed.</DefinitionHelp>; <DefinitionHelp id="mb-standard-error" label="SE">Standard error: the spread of the refitted estimates across the repeated player samples. It is not measurement error in an individual player's impact score.</DefinitionHelp>; <DefinitionHelp id="mb-post-selection" label="post-selection coverage">How intervals perform after the data have been used to choose a curve type. These bands keep the chosen type fixed and do not account for uncertainty from that choice.</DefinitionHelp>.</p>
        <p class="mb-small">Pointwise means one salary position at a time; conditional means the supplied scores are treated as fixed. A one-SE rule prefers a simpler model close to the best held-out error. REML tunes curve smoothness; model family means the type of curve. MSE is the average squared prediction error; lower means closer predictions on held-out players.</p>
        {data ? <><p>{data.definitions.uncertainty}</p><ul>{data.definitions.limitations.map(l => <li>{l}</li>)}</ul></> : <p>The salary/contribution match, complete season coverage and model evidence must pass validation before results can appear. This preview has no numerical findings.</p>}


    <section data-mb-million-details><h4>Extra $1 million: support and uncertainty</h4>
      <p class="mb-small" data-mb-million-context>{defaultMillion?.context}</p>
      <dl class="mb-million-evidence">
        <dt>Supported salary pair</dt><dd data-mb-million-anchor>{defaultMillion?.anchor}</dd>
        <dt>Fitted contribution difference</dt><dd data-mb-million-difference>{defaultMillion?.difference}</dd>
        <dt>Estimated range for this difference</dt><dd data-mb-million-range>{defaultMillion?.range}</dd>
        <dt>Nearby matched players</dt><dd data-mb-million-support>{defaultMillion?.support}</dd>
        <dt>Unrounded exported values</dt><dd data-mb-million-precision>{defaultMillion?.precision}</dd>
      </dl>
      <p class="mb-small">This is an existing supported pair on the league reference, not two observed players. Both salaries require enough nearby matched observations. The range uses the two fitted points jointly, treating supplied player scores as fixed; it does not measure uncertainty in an individual player's impact or include provider-score uncertainty. Displayed values are rounded; calculations use unrounded numbers. Source records and model details are in these notes.</p>
    </section>
<h4 id="mb-gap-size-calculation" tabindex="-1" data-reference-target>Gap size</h4>
<a class="mb-back-comparison" data-mb-return href="#mb-snapshot-title">Back to saved records</a>
<p>The typical league gap is the median distance from the salary-reference line: sort all matched players’ distances, ignoring which side of the line they are on, and take the middle distance (average the middle two for an even count). The selected player is included. For each metric/window, divide the saved signed contribution gap by this median absolute gap. Calculations use unrounded numbers; only the displayed values are rounded. The method is median-absolute-visible-gap-v1: no centering, normal-consistency multiplier or normal probabilities. The scale and count are shown beside a selected player and in the build records. Zero scales or ratios that cannot be represented safely are unavailable; no players are dropped and no alternative denominator is substituted.</p><p>This descriptive calculation needs no normal distribution assumption. It is not significance, salary-conditional rarity or uncertainty in a provider score. Gaps can vary more at some salaries than others. A stable denominator does not make the fitted salary curve resistant to outliers. Scores are relative to their own cohort: the same Gap size in different seasons or windows can represent different native contribution gaps and ranks.</p>
<h4 id="mb-percentile-calculation" tabindex="-1" data-reference-target>Gap percentile</h4>
<a class="mb-back-comparison" data-mb-return href="#mb-snapshot-title">Back to saved records</a>
<p>For each contribution measure and window, the percentile compares the player's gap from the salary reference with all eligible matched players in that view. Larger gaps rank higher. It counts every smaller gap and half of every exact tie, including the player, then divides by the full cohort size. Only the displayed percentile is rounded to one decimal.</p><p>Ranking uses the exact saved numbers for the gaps, not the rounded values on the page. A zero gap need not be the 50th percentile; the endpoints need not be 0 and 100. Filters preserve the full league cohort. Gaps can vary more at some salary levels than others. This rank does not measure how unusual a gap is, uncertainty, overall talent, causal value or return per dollar.</p>
